  "notes": "Etymology: from {形|かた}を{取|と}る (to take the shape of). The standard kanji is {象|かたど}る, but it can also be written as {模|かたど}る.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- 〜を{象|かたど}った＋{名詞|めいし}: something shaped/modeled after ...\n- 〜の{形|かたち}を{象|かたど}る: to imitate the shape of ...\n\nUSAGE: Often used in the past-participle form {象|かたど}った as a modifier (e.g., {星|ほし}を{象|かたど}ったデザイン). Common in art, design, and descriptions of kanji origins.",
